    <paragraph>Add and Subtract Polynomial Functions</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In each example, find ⓐ (f + g)(x) ⓑ (f + g)(2) ⓒ (f − g)(x) ⓓ (f − g)(−3).</paragraph>
    <exercise number="73" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = 2x^{2} - 4x + 1$$ and $$g(x) = 5x^{2} + 8x + 3$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$(f+g)(x)=7x2+4x+4(f+g)(x)=7x2+4x+4$$ ⓑ $$(f+g)(2)=40(f+g)(2)=40$$ ⓒ $$(f-g)(x)=-3x2-12x-2(f-g)(x)=-3x2-12x-2$$ ⓓ $$(f-g)(-3)=7(f-g)(-3)=7$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
