      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = 3x^{3} - x^{2} - 2x + 3$$ and $$g(x) = 3x^{3} - 7x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$(f+g)(x)=6x3-x2-9x+3(f+g)(x)=6x3-x2-9x+3$$ ⓑ $$(f+g)(2)=29(f+g)(2)=29$$ ⓒ $$(f-g)(x)=-x2+5x+3(f-g)(x)=-x2+5x+3$$ ⓓ $$(f-g)(-3)=-21(f-g)(-3)=-21$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
